    "migration": "MigrationAcceptanceTests migrates a scratch database to 20260906133421_CompleteProgramme, inserts a module, a section and two cohorts by SQL, migrates to 20260907155252_AuthorCurriculum, and asserts one published programme per key with modules and cohorts following it, populated revisions, twelve weeks at a cadence of two, a draft programme for the cohort key with no modules, and both key columns and the old index gone.",
    "packagedDeepLinks": "Against the Release build serving its own wwwroot on https://localhost:7341, /admin/programmes, /admin/programmes/{id}, /admin/modules/{id}, /admin/modules/{id}/preview and /admin/sections/{id} each returned 200 text/html carrying the Angular shell, while an anonymous GET /administration/curricula returned 401 rather than that document.",
    "developerDatabaseMigrate": "The developer Stewardship database applied 20260906133421_CompleteProgramme and 20260907155252_AuthorCurriculum with no pending migration left. It stood two migrations back, so this exercised the clean path; the backfill of existing keys is covered by the migration acceptance test above.",
    "staleReadRegression": "The cohort guard read a programme this context had itself tracked as a draft during an import in the same process, so a cohort created after an HTTP publication was refused. ProgrammeStore.CurriculumByKey now reads without tracking, which is what a check-then-act guard under the programme lock needs; three administration acceptance tests and the performance harness setup proved it."
